  "name": "Rotating field — 6p/36s",
  "description": "Multipole teaching motor: six poles, 36 teeth, three north–south pairs and a balanced three-phase distributed winding. Compare Stator only, PM only and Resultant fields. One electrical cycle covers 120 mechanical degrees. Begin with field lines, hidden flux-density colors, and 3 RPM playback. A numerical teaching design; not hardware validated.",
